[%#
  HDRY Parts Worksheet — candidate parts not yet imported.
  Printable: doubles as the import review sheet AND the shop-floor traveler
  for working through the print queue.
  Data generated by hdry_work/worksheet_data.py from real STL geometry.
%]
[% PageVersion = 'root/Documentation/hdry_parts_worksheet.tt,v 0.01 2026/09/02 shanta Exp shanta ' %]
[% IF c.session.debug_mode == 1 %][% PageVersion %][% END %]

[% META
   title = 'HDRY Parts Worksheet'
   description = 'Candidate un-imported HDRY STL parts, deduped by geometry, with proposed names and SKUs'
   category = 'Documentation'
   roles = 'admin,developer'
   TemplateType = 'worksheet'
   last_updated = '2026-09-02'
   page_version = '0.01'
   site_specific = 0
%]

<style>
.ws-table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 0.86em; }
.ws-table th, .ws-table td { border: 1px solid var(--border-color,#ccc); padding: 0.35em 0.5em; text-align: left; }
.ws-table th { background: var(--primary-color,#333); color: #fff; }
.ws-group td { background: var(--accent-color,#007bff); color:#fff; font-weight:bold; font-size:1.05em; }
.ws-num { text-align: right; white-space: nowrap; }
.ws-files { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--muted-color,#666); }
.ws-box { display:inline-block; width:1.1em; height:1.1em; border:1px solid var(--border-color,#666); vertical-align:middle; }
@media print { .no-print { display:none; } .ws-table { font-size: 9pt; } }
</style>

<h1>HDRY Parts Worksheet</h1>
<p class="doc-body">
Candidate STL parts found on disk that are <strong>not yet imported</strong> into
<code>printing_3d_models</code>. Duplicates removed by geometry match (volume + bounding
box + triangle count), so each row is one distinct mesh. Volumes and weights are
computed from the real STL &mdash; not carried over from a filename guess.
</p>

<p class="doc-body no-print">
Use this two ways: (1) <strong>import review</strong> &mdash; tick what to create, then
import once; (2) <strong>shop-floor traveler</strong> &mdash; print it and tick each row
as the part comes off the printer.
</p>

